    "basis": "Knowledge packet 2026-10-13 item E4, PROPOSED (not approved). Research bouillon_or_base_reconstituted_for_stock (SOURCE_SUPPORTED): Better Than Bouillon SRC-ST-16#a (1 teaspoon in 8 oz hot or boiling water = one 8-oz can of broth). Product-specific by design: there is no generic bouillon ratio (Knorr cubes 1 per 2 cups vs Herb-Ox and Maggi 1 per cup, SRC-ST-20#a, SRC-ST-17#a, SRC-ST-21#a), so this names one product. Chicken stock or broth only: a vegetable stock in a vegetarian dish needs a vegetable base (research condition), not this. Sodium: ATK suggests less base to lower salt without a number (SRC-ST-07#c): stated in the tradeoff, not applied. Input bounds 1/2-12 cups are engineering bounds."
  },
